  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "This article includes table pagination. Use the Search function in the tables to find your preferred field."
    },
    {
      "text": "The tunnel Nanolog Streaming Service (NSS) feed specifies the data from the tunnel logs that the NSS sends to the security information and event management (SIEM) system. You can configure an NSS feed by including one or more fields. The fields and their values display in the NSS feed output."
    },
    {
      "item": "View a sample tunnel log.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "\"Thu Jun 23 16:24:59 2022\",\"Tunnel Samples\",\"GRE\",\"NA(GRE Tunnel)\",\"new-gre\",\"10.66.89.115\",\"10.66.68.68\",\"0\",\"2\",\"3\",\"160\",\"753\",\"0\",\"7112472280601133057\"",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "The following tables display information about the tunnel fields and example values for those fields. If applicable, the tunnel fields are mapped to their corresponding columns in Tunnel Insights Logs (Data Explorer > Internet & SaaS > Tunnel Insights > Logs)."
    },
